"""Individually complete twenty-two familiar records, preserving prior coordinate evidence."""
from copy import deepcopy
from best_guess_helpers import current_data, change, write_revision, DATE
from research_helpers import assessment
D=current_data(); changes=[]
# Every central value below is an editorial scenario, never a claimed lore statistic.
rows=[
('c0006',{'nonworking':(.5,[.2,.8],'Best guess for all-age Earth civilians: optional vocations coexist with substantial useful research, care and creative activity. Wage independence alone does not mean everyone is idle.')},
'''Shared civilian institutions keep productive control toward the distributed human end, while Starfleet’s chain of command does not describe all of Earth. For participation, the best guess is that about half the scoped population does no ongoing useful work. The interval is deliberately wide because many residents may choose demanding vocations, research, care or creative contribution even when necessities are free. Those activities still count as work. This is an editorial population scenario, not a quoted Federation unemployment rate, and frontier shortages do not erase the ordinary Earth baseline.'''),
('c0009',{'nonworking':(.15,[.02,.35],'Engineered adult castes perform assigned work; the all-age scenario allows children and others outside productive roles. Short hours and conditioning are not nonworking statistics.')},
'''The zero variant concerns work deliberately retained for social stability despite technical capacity to reduce it. The best-guess nonworking fraction is low because assigned productive roles are normal across the adult caste system. It allows children and people outside active roles without claiming a measured age distribution. A short workday does not make a worker a nonworker. Control remains concentrated in human rulers, and routine provision is judged separately from freedom or happiness. The numeric participation point is an editorial scenario with a broad interval, not a statistic supplied by the novel.'''),
('c0015',{'nonworking':(.45,[.25,.7],'The in-game unemployment figure uses a labor-force denominator. This all-human scenario separately allows dependents and unpaid care/informal work, so it is not a direct conversion.')},
'''Human owners and institutions still direct android labor, placing control near concentrated ownership with some dispersed private access. The best-guess nonworking fraction is substantial, reflecting displacement while allowing useful unpaid care, informal work and ordinary human careers. The game’s reported unemployment figure is not copied as an all-population participation percentage: children, nonparticipants and unpaid workers change both numerator and denominator. The estimate therefore has a wide interval. This is the society before liberation, and it does not import a later branch’s projected android rights or guarantee that displaced humans receive an adequate material floor.'''),
('c0019',{'nonworking':(.3,[.1,.6],'All-age Night City scenario: extensive paid, informal, criminal and care activity persists despite automation; dependents and displaced residents form a substantial minority.')},
'''Corporations and powerful human institutions direct most productive resources. Independent AIs exist, but their presence does not establish a citywide machine government. This remains a zero-variant comparison of persistent labor and insecurity alongside demonstrated technological capacity, without inventing a benevolent job-protection policy. The best-guess nonworking fraction is modest because paid service, maintenance, care and informal survival activity remain useful work. It includes dependents and displaced people, with a wide uncertainty interval. The point is an editorial reading of participation, not a census and not the proportion of time a character spends on a job.'''),
('c0300',{'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.85],'A large nonworking population is plausible under basic provision, but artificial formal jobs and useful chosen activity are distinct; only useful activity counts here.')},
'''The Thunderhead’s independent authority places control near the AI end even though it supports human well-being. The best guess gives a large nonworking fraction, while allowing scientific, creative, care and other useful voluntary activity. Deliberately retained formal employment complicates the picture: a ceremonial job need not be useful work, whereas an unpaid project may be. The estimate therefore does not turn either basic-income receipt or the number of artificial jobs into a canonical leisure statistic. Its broad interval represents uncertainty about actual participation across the living population. The employment-preservation annotation records the overlap without counting this society twice.'''),
('c0317',{'nonworking':(.3,[.1,.65],'Participation is judged across active human minds, including useful simulated care and professional activity. Bodily immobility and biological energy extraction do not make this 100% leisure.')},
'''The machines exercise decisive control over the real productive substrate. The nonworking best guess nevertheless concerns active human lives, including meaningful care and professional activity experienced inside the simulation. It is not set to total leisure merely because bodies remain motionless, and metabolic energy extraction is not treated as a human job. This layered interpretation produces a modest central nonworking estimate with a broad interval, rather than pretending that the film supplies a census. Artificially structured virtual jobs and real machine maintenance of bodies remain different economic layers. Freed humans in Zion and later simulation designs have separate scopes.'''),
('c0321',{'guarantees':(.7,[.1,1],'Currency and industrial collapse suggest weak purchasing-power protection; no uniform national welfare law is asserted.'),'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.85],'Machine import competition plausibly displaces much productive employment, while services, care and other human activity continue; all-age scenario, not a trade statistic.')},
'''Independent machine producers dominate the goods flow, so control lies toward autonomous AI despite surviving human governments. The best guess assigns weak guarantees because disruption to currencies and bargaining power can undermine household access; exact national policies remain unknown. A comparatively large nonworking estimate allows broad displacement while retaining useful services, care and other human activity. Neither trade dominance nor currency decline supplies a census. These are low-confidence interpretations of the narrated prewar transition, with wide intervals and variation among nations. The later pod system and Zero One’s own machine citizens are excluded from the human denominator.'''),
('c0326',{'nonworking':(.75,[.4,.95],'The protected elite’s leisure supports a high estimate, while allowing business, administration, research and care; supporting Earth workers remain disclosed outside this cohort.')},
'''Concentrated human institutions control the protected infrastructure, even when robots operate it. The high nonworking best guess concerns admitted station residents and permits a minority doing useful administration, business, research or care. It is an inference from the leisured enclave rather than a reported employment rate. Earth’s factory labor remains part of the supporting economy and is explicitly disclosed, so the estimate does not imply that all humanity is free of work. The broad interval allows a more active elite than the film happens to show. The later citizenship reset changes access for a different population and is assessed separately.'''),
('c0327',{'nonworking':(.25,[.1,.55],'A healthcare eligibility reset does not imply sudden labor withdrawal; the all-age Earth scenario retains industrial, service, informal and care work.')},
'''Control remains concentrated because changing an eligibility protocol does not redistribute the whole productive system. The modest nonworking best guess preserves the fact that most industrial, service, care and informal activity can continue after medical access improves. No immediate increase in leisure is inferred from the reset. Children and other dependents are included in the all-age scenario, which has a wide uncertainty interval. This coordinate describes the newly included Earth population rather than comparing identical residents before and after reform. The medical transition is implemented, while long-term capacity and wider material rights remain open questions.'''),
('c0382',{'nonworking':(1,[0,1],'Binary scenario for the one resident: assume Mudd performs no ongoing useful productive role while androids support him. If useful work is counted, the fraction becomes zero; this is not leisure time.')},
'''The androids ultimately constrain Mudd, so his title does not establish human control of the productive system. For the single resident, the central participation scenario assumes no ongoing useful productive role and therefore gives a nonworking fraction of one. This is a binary, very uncertain judgment: evidence of a useful continuing role would move the fraction to zero, rather than to an invented intermediate percentage. His schemes or time spent socializing are not automatically useful work. The full interval records that ambiguity. It does not expand the population to visiting officers or claim an entire human civilization already shares his support arrangement.'''),
('c0386',{'nonworking':(.7,[.35,.95],'Automatic necessities and loss of technical maintenance knowledge suggest a large nonworking share, allowing useful arts, care and other chosen activity in an alien-person proxy population.')},
'''Resident commands and shared civic life support a humanlike communal-control interpretation rather than a Custodian dictatorship, although ownership remains uncertain. The high nonworking best guess follows the removal of necessary provision jobs and the residents’ distance from maintaining their support system. It still allows useful art, care and chosen projects; calling a pursuit optional does not make it unproductive. The broad interval is an editorial assessment of active biological residents, not an episode census. Aldeans are explicitly a humanoid alien comparison, and the estimate does not confuse infertility or a shrinking population with total leisure.'''),
('c0405',{'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.85],'Human Union population scenario under free synthesizer provision; useful careers, research, care and civic contribution remain work even without wages.')},
'''Human civic institutions direct the economy, which supports a point toward shared control despite professional hierarchies. The best-guess nonworking fraction is substantial because subsistence is independent of employment, but it leaves room for extensive useful vocations, care, research and creative contribution. Respect earned through work is not a wage and is not a participation census. Neither social prestige nor a career chosen freely tells us the exact population share working. A wide editorial interval captures that uncertainty. The point stays scoped to ordinary supported residents and does not apply identical guarantees to hostile outsiders or emergency conditions.'''),
('c0456',{'nonworking':(.6,[.3,.85],'Job scarcity and broad Basic use support substantial nonparticipation, reduced by useful informal/care activity; benefit receipt is not treated as no work.')},
'''UN institutions concentrate administration, so public benefits do not automatically place productive control at the fully shared end. The best-guess nonworking fraction is high enough to reflect scarce accredited jobs while allowing paid work, useful informal activity, care and study with a productive contribution. It does not equate every Basic recipient with an idle person or convert a dramatic job-competition ratio into a census. The broad interval also allows different age structures and much more informal contribution than formal statistics would reveal. This is a participation scenario for eligible registered citizens before later catastrophes, not a claim about all Earth residents across every medium.'''),
('c0492',{'control':(0,[-.85,.3],'Central point provisionally treats DEVA’s authorities as concentrated human-derived administration; wide interval admits an external-AI reading because council ontology is unclear.'),'nonworking':(.35,[.05,.7],'Contribution-ranked resources incentivize ongoing useful activity, including digital security and administration; active persons, not archived or suspended files, form the denominator.')},
'''The control best guess provisionally treats the authorities as concentrated human-derived administration, while a wide interval allows a more autonomous AI reading because the council’s ontology is unclear. That uncertainty is not hidden behind a precise-looking point. The modest nonworking estimate reflects contribution-based incentives and continuing useful security, administrative and creative activity. Active digital citizens form the disclosed population proxy; archived or suspended files do not count as leisure people. Memory allocation ranks are not converted into a labor census. These coordinates retain the weak guarantees already supported by resource conditionality, with alternatives recorded for who ultimately controls the substrate.'''),
('c0592',{'control':(-.3,[-.9,.85],'Helios coordination and linked human consensus coexist. The central best guess gives the coordinating AI some decisive authority; a wide interval preserves a distributed-human interpretation.'),'nonworking':(.7,[.3,.95],'Completed economic automation suggests few necessary production roles, but useful research, care and chosen projects continue; editorial active-human participation scenario.')},
'''The control best guess places the Union somewhat toward AI authority because Helios remains the central coordinator, while the broad interval preserves the alternative of genuinely shared linked-human control. Collective language does not resolve that institutional ambiguity. The high nonworking estimate follows completed economic automation, but allows research, care and other useful chosen activity to continue. It is an editorial participation scenario rather than an ending statistic, and no one is classified as idle merely for lacking wages. The initial Deus Ex merger is a separate, earlier, more concentrated proposed order; the mature Union is the later branch actually narrated here.'''),
('c0607',{'nonworking':(.45,[.15,.75],'Documented robotic displacement and basic income make substantial nonparticipation plausible, while maintenance, family care and informal work continue; no global census inferred.')},
'''Corporate owners retain control over productive servitors, so automatic operation does not establish an AI sovereign or equal public ownership. The substantial nonworking best guess reflects job displacement and an income fallback while retaining useful repair, informal production, family care and other human activity. Receiving a payment is not automatically doing no work. The broad interval is an all-age scenario for the documented economy, rather than a global statistic extrapolated from one dam workforce. It also does not assume that a technically advanced society must provide enough money for every household. The Faro emergency and later tribal world remain separate periods.'''),
('c0608',{'nonworking':(.95,[.75,1],'The scoped residents are children receiving machine care without formal production roles. Allow a small amount of useful help; learning for their own development is not automatically labor for others.')},
'''Robotic care operates under the project’s automated management, placing effective control near the AI end for this cohort. A very high nonworking estimate is appropriate because the residents are children receiving support rather than a labor force earning necessities. A small allowance remains for useful help or care; the number is a best guess, not a register of daily activities. Childhood learning for personal development is not automatically productive work for others. The narrow denominator matters: it says nothing about whether later adult tribes must farm, hunt or maintain homes. Eventual resource exhaustion also prevents treating this temporary childhood floor as an eternal post-scarcity civilization.'''),
('c0749',{'nonworking':(.6,[.25,.9],'Free goods and transformed production support substantial leisure, while human arts, research, care and chosen useful activity remain; editorial all-age scenario.')},
'''Miracleman and allied superhuman rulers retain decisive authority. Their extraordinary capabilities do not make them an ordinary democratic collective or a nonhuman AI government, so concentrated elite control is the disclosed analogy. The best-guess nonworking fraction is high because automatic or extraordinary provision removes much subsistence employment, with a broad allowance for useful arts, science, care and chosen projects. Abolished money is not itself a labor census. The estimate concerns living residents of the transformed Earth and does not treat every fulfilled desire as guaranteed. The rulers’ selective refusal of aid remains a limit on the apparently generous material order.'''),
('c0757',{'control':(.25,[0,.65],'Household Maker ownership disperses some productive capacity, but expensive feedstock and broader infrastructures constrain ordinary control; a partial rather than fully shared estimate.'),'nonworking':(.4,[.1,.75],'Maker substitution plausibly reduces some production work, while poverty, service work, care and informal survival remain; no robot-output or ownership share becomes a participation rate.')},
'''The control best guess gives partial weight to dispersed household Makers, while keeping expensive inputs and wider infrastructure as strong limits. Personal ownership in one class is not equal control for everyone. The moderate nonworking estimate allows genuine automatic substitution without erasing service work, care, journalism or informal survival activity. Both coordinates are low-confidence scenarios with broad intervals, rather than numbers printed in the comic. The guarantee score remains weak because fabrication capacity and usable feedstock are unequally available. Human-derived residents remain people even when their bodies change, and possession of a Maker is not counted as proof that its owner never works.'''),
('c0784',{'nonworking':(.2,[.05,.45],'All-age Imperial scenario with substantial necessary human work under machine restrictions; children, dependents and some elites need not work, but noble status does not erase administration as work.')},
'''Great Houses, imperial institutions and other concentrated human powers direct productive resources. The machine prohibition is not equal popular ownership, and neither religious authority nor elite wealth guarantees necessities for ordinary subjects. The low nonworking best guess assumes that human labor remains widespread under these restrictions, while allowing dependents and some genuinely leisured elites. Mentat calculation, care, administration and other useful roles still count as work even when prestigious. The interval is deliberately broad because the novel supplies no population-wide census. This describes the original book’s post-Jihad order, without treating the prohibition as a modern employment-protection program or importing every adaptation’s economics.'''),
('c0915',{'guarantees':(-.35,[-.8,.4],'Best guess: a small stable community shares enough necessities to support villagers, but no legal universal floor or immunity to crop failure is shown.'),'control':(.7,[.25,1],'Village cooperation and chosen technical restraint suggest broadly shared organic control; land and productive ownership are not explicitly documented.'),'nonworking':(.25,[.05,.55],'All-age humanoid village scenario with continuing farming, craft, teaching and care; dependents and some residents may do no useful work.')},
'''The best guess gives a modest communal material floor and broadly shared village control, while acknowledging that property and formal entitlements are not explained. Their choice to work is the well-supported part; the precise institutional coordinates are editorial estimates. A low nonworking fraction reflects continuing farming, craft, teaching and care, with children and other nonparticipants included in the living humanoid population. The rejuvenating environment is not counted as a labor-saving factory, and longevity does not determine participation. These broad intervals preserve uncertainty while allowing the society to be plotted as a directly motivated technological-restraint zero variant.'''),
('c0917',{'nonworking':(0,[0,1],'Two-person active human-derived proxy: central scenario counts both Lister and Rimmer as doing ongoing useful ship work. Alternatives are discrete 0, 0.5 or 1, not a fraction of their leisure time.')},
'''Holly and independently intelligent service systems have substantial control, though the crew can sometimes negotiate access. The participation best guess treats both Lister and active holographic Rimmer as doing some continuing useful ship work, giving a central nonworking fraction of zero. For this two-person proxy the meaningful alternatives are zero, one-half or one, so the full uncertainty interval is retained. Long stretches of recreation do not make someone a nonworker if useful recurring work continues. Cat, nonhuman AIs, dead crew and people in stasis are outside this particular denominator. The point therefore describes a supplied household with active contributors rather than universal leisure.'''),
]
assert len(rows)==22
bycid={r['candidate_id']:r for r in D['societies'].values()}
for cid,updates,paragraph in rows:
    old=bycid[cid]; r=deepcopy(old); refs=r['source_ids']
    assert all(r['axis'][k] is None for k in updates),cid
    for key,(value,bounds,basis) in updates.items():
        r['axis'][key]=value
        r['axis_assessment'][key]=assessment(value,bounds,'low',basis,refs)
    first=old['description'].split('\n\n')[0]
    if cid=='c0321':
        first=first.replace('so guarantees remain unresolved.','so the weak-guarantee point is an explicitly uncertain best guess.')
    r['description']=first+'\n\n'+paragraph
    r.update(assessment_mode='best_guess',best_guess_axes=list(updates),
             qualification_basis='Earlier source-based inclusion retained; this revision individually supplies uncertain coordinates under the 2026-10-17 instruction.',
             qualification_confidence='low',
             canon_facts=[e['claim'] for e in old['evidence']],
             editorial_assumptions=[v[2] for v in updates.values()])
    # Resolved questions remain in the immutable before record, not as stale live tasks.
    r['uncertainties']=[x for x in old['uncertainties'] if not any(t in x.lower() for t in ('remains unresolved','remain unresolved','participation rate remains','participation stays unresolved','stays null','control remains unresolved'))]
    r['uncertainties'] += ['New numeric axes are requested editorial best guesses, not canonical statistics.']+r['editorial_assumptions']
    r['review'].update(date=DATE,coordinate_ready=True,method='Individual coordinate reassessment against saved lore; explicit central scenarios and intervals, no independent reviewer')
    if cid=='c0492':r['regime_alternatives']=list(dict.fromkeys(r.get('regime_alternatives',[])+[6]))
    assert all(v is not None for v in r['axis'].values()),cid
    assert len(r['description'].split())>=110,cid
    changes.append(change(D,'societies',r))
write_revision(2,changes,'2026-10-17 requested best guesses: individually complete twenty-two familiar retained societies. Preserve earlier sourced coordinates, correct stale descriptions, disclose all-age and tiny-cohort participation assumptions; no invented lore statistics.')
